module gunbc.fixture_render_selection_seed_growth

import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// FORWARD-FREEZE RECEIPT for floor repair C1 (docs/plans/floor-time-attribution-2026-10-02.md):
// the fixture compile instruments render only the modules their reader reads.
//
// WHAT THE CHANGE IS. compile_dag_rust_emit_check and compile_dag_diagnostic_census compiled the
// fixture's whole live import closure, which is unchanged, and then rendered Rust for EVERY
// module of it. The emit check reads one emitted file. The census reads diagnostics, among them
// the emit refusals of the modules it renders. Every other rendered module was demanded by no
// consumer (DESIGN section 2: delete redundant demand, do not cache it). The selection is the
// existing RenderSelectedMirrors arm of v1.compiler.artifact RustModuleRenderSelection, which
// required_regen_host already uses in production. No pipeline stage is edited.
//
// CORRECTED 2026-10-23 (gunbc#14909, the census render-subject fix): THE CENSUS NO LONGER TAKES
// THIS ROUTE AT ALL. The census runs on the compiled graph's diagnostics and requests NO render
// subject; its branch of the fixture compile now goes through compile_fixture_rendering_nothing
// (enumerated below) with an EMPTY RenderSelectedMirrors selection, never through
// fixture_render_selection. The sentence above saying compile_fixture_rendering_only_what_is_read
// is "the one route both instruments now take" describes this receipt's original scope and is
// true only of the emit check and the agreement receipt today. fixture_render_selection stays
// live for those two consumers; its census-side NoFixtureModuleInClosure refusal -- which made
// parse-error fixtures report -1 instead of their located parse diagnostics, because a parse
// failure precedes any module declaration to select -- is gone with the census's render demand.
// The two per-thread counters below make a census-side widening to either render shape
// (whole-graph, or a non-empty selected list) a control failure in
// src/v1/stage0/tests/census_no_render_subject_control.rs; their rung is stated honestly there
// (a cargo test no CI step runs, gunbc.rung_drop v1_required_lanes_withdrawn).
//
// HAND-ITEM DELTA: +10 citable declarations in v1_compiler.cli_run and v1_compiler, plus one
// uncitable Display impl listed in gunbc.seed_growth_admission seed_growth_uncitable_item_keys,
// plus two uncitable thread_local statics (EVERY_MODULE_RENDER_CALLS,
// NON_EMPTY_SELECTED_RENDER_CALLS -- counters are not declarations; named so this receipt does
// not under-report its own growth, same practice as gunbc.census_memo_seed_growth's seven) and
// one new integration test file src/v1/stage0/tests/census_no_render_subject_control.rs. Two enum
// variants are added and are not declarations: v1_interpreter InterpError FixtureRenderRefused
// and v1_compiler.cli_run WitnessRuntimeCause FixtureRenderRefused. Both are the typed refusal
// arm, and WitnessRuntimeCause is total over InterpError. They are named here so the receipt does
// not under-report its own growth.
data fixture_render_selection_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "FIXTURE_SOURCE_PATH", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "compile_fixture_rendering_only_what_is_read", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "fixture_render_selection", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "FixtureRenderRefusal", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "RenderSelectionAgreementFixture", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "RENDER_SELECTION_AGREEMENT_FIXTURES", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "render_selection_agreement_receipt", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.emit_host", decl_name: "compile_fixture_rendering_nothing", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_compiler_compile", decl_name: "every_module_render_calls", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_compiler_compile", decl_name: "non_empty_selected_render_calls", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "The two instruments are host builtins that call the seed's compile pipeline synchronously, so the place to stop rendering what nobody reads is the host call site. A .dag-side selection would have to name a compile the substrate cannot represent, which is the boundary gunbc.census_memo_seed_growth records for the memo on the same builtins. compile_fixture_rendering_only_what_is_read is the route the emit check and the agreement receipt take. fixture_render_selection DERIVES the render set from the compiled graph: the modules spanned in FIXTURE_SOURCE_PATH, plus the closure module whose emitted path is the read path. So the selection cannot name a module outside the closure. FixtureRenderRefusal is the typed refusal arm: no fixture module in the closure, or a clean compile that emitted no file at the read path. That refusal replaced both a fall back to rendering every module and a silent false. render_selection_agreement_receipt over RENDER_SELECTION_AGREEMENT_FIXTURES (rows of RenderSelectionAgreementFixture) is the enrolled control that the required floor runs on every run. It is the one remaining execution of the full render. It refuses the floor when the read bytes, the diagnostics or the narrowing route disagree, and its import-free fixture is the authorable red for the route. SINCE gunbc#14909 (the census render-subject fix) THE CENSUS TAKES A THIRD ROUTE that needs no selection at all: compile_fixture_rendering_nothing compiles the same fixed point and emits with an EMPTY RenderSelectedMirrors, because the census consumes only the compiled graph's diagnostics and demanded no render subject -- a demanded one was the bug: its NoFixtureModuleInClosure refusal made parse-error fixtures report -1 instead of the located parse diagnostics the fleet witnesses exist to check. every_module_render_calls and non_empty_selected_render_calls are the counters that make any census-side widening back to a render (whole-graph, or a non-empty selected list) a control failure; they are read only by src/v1/stage0/tests/census_no_render_subject_control.rs, whose rung (a cargo test no CI step runs; gunbc.rung_drop v1_required_lanes_withdrawn) the file states itself. The counters sit at emit_resolved_for_target_selected, where every selection arrives whatever entry point the caller used, and they are per-thread because cargo test runs one file's tests in parallel threads of one process.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete all ten when compile_dag_rust_emit_check and compile_dag_diagnostic_census are MODELED operations rather than host builtins. At that point the render set is the demand of the modeled reader, derived by the substrate. The receipt and its fixtures migrate with the instruments or are deleted with them; they never stand beside a modeled sibling. The 2026-10-23 additions retire on the same trigger: compile_fixture_rendering_nothing is the census branch of the same builtins, and the two counters exist only to police a widening the modeled reader would make impossible by construction -- when the census is modeled, its demand IS the render set, and a hand-carried counter beside it is the duplicated authority this receipt's own single-authority argument refuses.",
  current_boundary: "Confined to the two fixture instruments and the one required-floor receipt. The narrowing is a stated semantic change, not an invisible one. A corpus module in a fixture's closure is no longer rendered, so its own per-module emit refusal no longer reaches the census rows or the emit check's hard-diagnostic gate. SINCE gunbc#14909 THE CENSUS RENDERS NOTHING FROM THE FIXTURE AT ALL: the fixture's own modules are no longer rendered by the census either, so per-module emit refusals of the fixture's own modules no longer reach the census rows. What still reaches them: every diagnostic the compiled fixed point produces (parse, resolve, type, admission, and the transport/record/admission emit classes the fixed-point compile itself computes) — the census keeps reporting the located diagnostics its witnesses exist to check. What no longer can arrive in census rows: only classes produced by the per-module render step itself — EmittedSymbolCollision, ModuleFilenameCollision, NativeEffectRealizationRefused, ReferenceDerivedImportExportUnproven, UnlistedImportUse (EmittedSymbolCollision's fleet witness consumes it through compile_dag_rust_emit_check, which still renders its read-path module and is unchanged). NO CENSUS-CONSUMING FLEET WITNESS ASSERTS ANY OF THE FIVE; the four that assert emit-path classes through the census — test/claim/transport_emission_not_modeled_witness, transport_field_refusal_witness, pipeline_transport_emit_rest_shell_witness, record_emission_candidate_set_witness — assert classes the fixed-point compile still produces. None of the four carries a gunbc test label; each is re-derived per head by its claim_batch entry — claim_batch --wet --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/<witness>.dag --functions <the witness's cell list> — and that comparison, run 2026-10-23 on this PR's exact head and base, is a one-off observation recorded in the PR's receipt comments, not an instrument and not part of this boundary; the boundary claim itself rests only on the enumeration above (no census-consuming witness asserts a render-step class, which any reader can re-derive by grep over dag/test/claim/ and the census instrument's cells). Whole-graph emit checks run before selection and are unchanged. A corpus module's own emission is the subject of the generated-artifact lanes, which render it for real. A future census witness that asserts one of the five render-step classes would read vacuously absent — that is the live boundary of this narrowing, recorded here rather than discovered by a green cell."
}
